hatchet = Hatchet(debug=True)
@hatchet.workflow()
class WorkflowOne:
@hatchet.step()
async def step(self, context: Context):
return {"test1": "test1"}
@hatchet.workflow()
class WorkflowTwo:
@hatchet.step()
async def step(self, context: Context):
return {"test2": "test2"}
worker = hatchet.worker('test-worker')
...
Workers can be started by calling either
`worker.start` or
`worker.async_start`.
We recommend that
`worker.start` is the last call made when running a worker.
The
`worker.start` method is blocking, while
`worker.async_start` can be awaited or started via
`asyncio.create_task`.
